# Cursor Rules for Ecotone

Read AGENTS.md in the project root before writing code, and docs/coding-conventions.md for the rules in full.

Nothing else belongs in this file. A rule stated here is a second copy that drifts from the one in
docs/coding-conventions.md — this file said `EcotoneLite::bootstrapForTesting()`, which does not exist, and
demanded `@param`/`@return` PHPDoc, which convention 6 forbids.
